abstract: >-
  A machine-checked characterization of the zero fibre of a finite positively
  weighted retained-difference operator over the rationals, together with a
  companion philosophy-of-mathematics paper. The formal artifact proves the
  edge and connected-component characterizations, closure of the zero locus,
  and the induced equivalence relation, and includes executable boundary
  witnesses.
keywords:
  - zero fibre
  - retained difference
  - graph Laplacian
  - Dirichlet energy
  - equivalence relation
  - formal verification
  - Rocq
  - Coq
  - philosophy of mathematics
